research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-2026-10-23/research-eft-experiments.md:26:The exact page-level sources are [the QFT category](../../library/quantum-field-theory/_category.md), [the Gaussian heavy-field page](../../library/quantum-field-theory-mathematics/qftx-heavy-field-eft.md), [the causal-renormalization page](../../library/quantum-field-theory-mathematics/qftx-causal-renormalization.md), [the on-shell-amplitudes page](../../library/quantum-field-theory-mathematics/qftx-on-shell-amplitudes.md), [the anomaly-cocycles page](../../library/quantum-field-theory-mathematics/qftx-anomaly-cocycles.md), and [the experiment carrier](../../items/exp-qft-fan-electron-moment-2022.md). The existing QFT scaffold itself expressly says it does not supply a general Wilsonian flow, running coefficients, matching conditions, or generic EFT truncation errors; see `physics/research/extended-frameworks-2026-10-03/quantum-field-theory/prose-scaffold.md`, “Renormalization has several meanings” and the EFT paragraph.
research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-2026-10-23/research-eft-experiments.md:28:Purely mathematical prerequisite pages available from the root library include [Formal Power Series](../../../library/combinatorics/formal-power-series.md) (`thm-formal-composition-laws`, `thm-formal-compositional-inverse`), [Lie Groups, Invariant Fields, and the Exponential Map](../../../library/lie-theory/lie-groups-invariant-fields-and-the-exponential-map.md), [Compact Lie Groups, Maximal Tori, and Peter–Weyl Theory](../../../library/lie-theory/compact-lie-groups-maximal-tori-and-peter-weyl-theory.md), [Reductive Affine Invariant Theory and Geometric Quotients](../../../library/algebraic-geometry/reductive-affine-invariant-theory-and-geometric-quotients.md), [Euclidean Ordinary Differential Equations with Smooth Dependence](../../../library/differential-geometry/euclidean-ordinary-differential-equations-with-smooth-dependence.md) (`thm-picard-lindelof-local-existence-and-uniqueness`), [Distributions, Test Functions and Differentiation](../../../library/functional-analysis/distributions-test-functions-and-differentiation.md) (`thm-distributions-supported-at-one-point`), [Tempered Distributions and the Fourier Transform](../../../library/functional-analysis/tempered-distributions-and-the-fourier-transform.md), [Spectral Measures and Borel Functional Calculus](../../../library/functional-analysis/spectral-measures-and-borel-functional-calculus.md), [Contour Integration](../../../library/complex-analysis/contour-integration.md), and [The Residue Theorem](../../../library/complex-analysis/the-residue-theorem.md). Their current carriers and any pinned/imported paths must be checked when the builder makes the exact plan. Planned suppliers remain planned; none of these references may be used to imply an EFT-specific theorem that they do not state.
research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-2026-10-23/research-eft-experiments.md:53:| 6 | `aqft-eft-anomalies` / `aqft-eft-anomalies-examples` | Threshold/anomaly matching and Wess–Zumino EFT interface; follow the gauge and symmetry researchers' exact anomaly supplier pages and the stated `qftx` mathematical boundary. |
research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-2026-10-23/research-eft-experiments.md:61:Definitions should distinguish the microscopic model, its light fields, heavy fields/thresholds, regulator, Wilsonian scale `mu`, heavy mass/scale `M`, external energy `E`, and EFT cutoff `Lambda`; do not use those three scales interchangeably. Fix spacetime, signature, units, field spaces/representations, regularity, gauge/flavor symmetries, and normalization of the action. Define a Wilsonian action as a functional integral or rigorously specified finite-regulator pushforward over a declared high-mode sector. Define a local derivative expansion and its truncation as an asymptotic/organized approximation with named power-counting assumptions, not as a convergent series by default. Keep it distinct from a 1PI effective action and from a renormalized time-ordered product.
research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-2026-10-23/research-eft-experiments.md:63:Candidate items: `def-aqft-model-and-scale-data`; `def-aqft-wilsonian-action`; `def-aqft-derivative-expansion-and-truncation`; `texp-aqft-finite-heavy-scalar-matching`; and `ex-aqft-gaussian-shell-matching` on the B page. The model item should explicitly state any functional measure or finite regulator and any physical adoptions. A thought-experiment result can derive a matching formula only conditionally on that construction; a mathematical proposition can handle the finite Gaussian integral without claiming it is nature's theory.
research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-2026-10-23/research-eft-experiments.md:65:The first exact result should be the finite Gaussian match already proved in `lem-qftx-finite-heavy-gaussian-square` and `thm-qftx-heavy-derivative-bound`, with all spectral-band, positivity, normalization, and units hypotheses copied exactly. Add a separate proposition showing successive Gaussian shells compose via `prop-qftx-finite-gaussian-shell-semigroup`; do not infer a differentiable flow from that composition. `thm-qftx-truncated-rg-ode` may illustrate the solution of a given one-coupling truncation, only with its exact caveat that it neither supplies a coefficient nor bounds higher orders.
research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-2026-10-23/research-eft-experiments.md:73:The operator basis is a quotient, not merely a list: specify the vector space of local monomials at fixed field content/order, the ideal/subspace of algebraic, Fierz, integration-by-parts/total-derivative, and leading-equations-of-motion relations being imposed, plus any global/gauge symmetry relations. Specify boundary conditions or compact-support assumptions under which total derivatives disappear from the action. A field redefinition must be a local invertible formal map with identity leading term, its order in `1/Lambda`, and the precise observable/S-matrix equivalence statement at the retained order. Do not use a classical EOM identity to assert equivalence of arbitrary off-shell Green functions or ignore a quantum Jacobian/anomaly premise.
research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-2026-10-23/research-eft-experiments.md:79:Power counting must use the chosen counting scheme. Canonical dimension counting for a weakly coupled linear EFT, chiral/loop counting in HEFT, and a multi-scale SCET expansion are different systems. Each result must identify the order retained and which loops, insertions, and interferences contribute at that order. An `O(E^n/Lambda^n)` label needs a norm/observable domain and a bound or an explicitly formal asymptotic interpretation; power counting alone is not a numerical error estimate.
research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-2026-10-23/research-eft-experiments.md:83:Define a renormalization scheme, scale-dependent coefficient vector, beta function/anomalous-dimension matrix, and matching map. Matching should equate a declared set of renormalized low-energy amplitudes/Green functions in the full and effective theories at a scale near a specified threshold, with identical IR regulators and renormalization conventions; it should state loop order, operator basis, mass expansion, and finite terms. Separate matching (changing field content/threshold) from running (evolving coefficients within one EFT). For several thresholds, state the ordered composition of matching and evolution maps.
research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-2026-10-23/research-eft-experiments.md:85:Candidate items: `def-aqft-scheme-and-wilson-coefficients`; `def-aqft-threshold-matching-map`; `prop-aqft-matching-and-running-scale-independence`; `thm-aqft-truncated-coupled-rge-wellposedness`; `ex-aqft-qed-threshold-matching`; and a SUSY threshold example coordinated with the supersymmetry researcher. A one-loop SMEFT RGE coefficient is only a theorem after the basis, flavor assumptions, regulator/subtraction scheme, and computed matrix entries are explicit. The `Jenkins–Manohar–Trott` three-paper result gives one-loop dimension-six running for its assumptions; it is an external statement to reproduce or import only through the approved exact source protocol.
research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-2026-10-23/research-eft-experiments.md:87:Small mathematical prerequisites: existence and uniqueness for finite-dimensional locally Lipschitz ODEs (already used by `thm-qftx-truncated-rg-ode`), matrix exponential/ordered evolution for the stated coefficient system, and formal power series for perturbative order bookkeeping. The larger missing mathematical/physical supplier is a local derivation of matching coefficients from a selected UV model and the corresponding full anomalous-dimension matrix. The existing formal scalar scale cocycle is not a substitute for this SMEFT calculation.
research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-2026-10-23/research-eft-experiments.md:93:For SMEFT, define the Standard Model gauge group and every representation, the linearly transforming Higgs doublet, the exact global/flavor/baryon/lepton assumptions, and a finite operator order. For HEFT/electroweak chiral EFT, define the nonlinear Goldstone coordinate/map for the chosen coset, the physical scalar singlet, its transformation law, and the chiral/loop power counting. State a concrete parameterization and coordinate patch for Goldstone fields when needed; do not identify it with an ordinary linear Higgs doublet by notation alone.
research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-2026-10-23/research-eft-experiments.md:95:Candidate items: `post-aqft-smeft-model`; `def-aqft-warsaw-basis-contract`; `post-aqft-heft-model`; `def-aqft-chiral-power-counting`; `prop-aqft-smeft-as-restricted-heft-branch`; and `ex-aqft-smeft-heft-observable-map`. A restricted-branch proposition must list the coefficient/analyticity relations that realize the chosen linear-Higgs model inside the chosen HEFT parameterization. It must not assert that a finite SMEFT truncation parameterizes every HEFT or that every HEFT point has a weakly coupled UV completion.
research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-2026-10-23/research-eft-experiments.md:97:`Grzadkowski et al. 2010` is the Warsaw-basis source, with the paper's assumptions about baryon number and flavor made explicit. `Buchalla, Cata, Krause 2015` supplies a systematic electroweak chiral/HEFT Lagrangian and loop power counting at NLO. The current library has neither classification as an exact local item. The local author must prove any selected reduction/correspondence or limit the page to definitions and source-faithful postulates with proof obligations left open.
research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-2026-10-23/research-eft-experiments.md:101:Define the external stable states, LSZ/scattering data if such a construction is available, Mandelstam variables, crossing action, partial-wave normalization, amplitude analytic domain, poles/cuts, IR regulator and subtraction point. Start with a massive, gapped scalar elastic channel with a finite forward limit and an explicitly stated real-analytic, crossing-symmetric, unitary amplitude and polynomial high-energy bound. Derive one forward dispersion inequality in that narrow setting. Only after this base result may the scaffold add spinning/multifield channels, nonforward bounds, massless gauge particles or gravity.
research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-2026-10-23/research-eft-experiments.md:103:Candidate items: `def-aqft-scattering-amplitude-input`; `lem-aqft-crossing-even-forward-amplitude`; `thm-aqft-gapped-scalar-forward-positivity`; `def-aqft-truncated-amplitude-bootstrap-problem`; `prop-aqft-finite-truncated-bootstrap-constraints`; and `ex-aqft-scalar-positivity-bound`. The B page should show both an allowed and a forbidden Wilson-coefficient region under exactly the same assumptions. `thm-qftx-rational-bcfw-residue` is reusable only for its conditional rational tree recursion. The new positivity proof still owes the contour argument, crossing/symmetrization, pole subtraction, subtractions at infinity, optical-theorem spectral sign, and low-energy coefficient identification.
research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-2026-10-23/research-eft-experiments.md:107:### A6 — EFT gauge and anomaly interface (`aqft-eft-anomalies`)
research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-2026-10-23/research-eft-experiments.md:109:This page is an interface, not a substitute for the gauge specialist's anomaly work. Define local gauge anomaly, anomaly polynomial/descent data, background/global symmetry anomaly, admissible counterterm, and Wess–Zumino functional in the exact chosen model. Distinguish an inconsistent gauge redundancy (which blocks the proposed quantum gauge theory absent a specified cancellation mechanism) from a global 't Hooft anomaly that an infrared effective theory must reproduce. When integrating out heavy chiral matter, state how its mass is generated and what degrees of freedom, Goldstone fields, or topological terms remain; ordinary power-suppressed decoupling is not automatic for anomaly data.
research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-2026-10-23/research-eft-experiments.md:111:Candidate items: `def-aqft-anomaly-matching-data`; `prop-aqft-heavy-chiral-threshold-wess-zumino-match`; and `ex-aqft-heavy-fermion-anomaly-threshold`, but only after the gauge/anomaly researcher supplies the exact local definitions, anomaly normalization, and hypotheses. Reuse `qftx-bv-brst`, `qftx-anomaly-cocycles`, and `def-qftx-chiral-anomaly-interface` at their actual Abelian/scalar or purely mathematical interfaces. `D'Hoker–Farhi` and Wess–Zumino/Witten sources are candidate literature inputs; any coefficient-level statement must identify representations, symmetry breaking, regulator, descent convention, and admissible local counterterms. The current local QFT item does not prove the general non-Abelian threshold-matching statement.
research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-2026-10-23/research-eft-experiments.md:117:Candidate items: `def-aqft-susy-wilsonian-action`; `prop-aqft-supersymmetric-threshold-matching`; `thm-aqft-wilsonian-superpotential-nonrenormalization` (only with the regulator, field content, gauge invariance, perturbative scope, and chiral/holomorphic definitions of the selected source); and `ex-aqft-soft-breaking-effective-operator`. Weinberg's perturbative theorem is a candidate source for the nonrenormalization obligation: it allows arbitrary gauge-invariant holomorphic `F(Phi,W)` in the Wilsonian Lagrangian, apart from one-loop gauge-coupling renormalization, subject to a cutoff preserving supersymmetry and gauge invariance. It is not a claim about nonperturbative corrections, arbitrary 1PI actions, or a model-independent absence of all running. Use the physical BPS bridge only after the localization/BPS researcher establishes it; the existing mathematical CoHA contract explicitly demands an additional dictionary and proves no physical index identity.
research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-2026-10-23/research-eft-experiments.md:125:| Reuse `exp-qft-fan-electron-moment-2022` on `qft-x03-examples` | One-electron cryogenic Penning-trap measurement; alternating cyclotron/anomaly quantum-jump spectroscopy; axial frequency detection; fitted frequencies; field drift, cyclotron broadening and cavity corrections; 11 weighted determinations; reported `g/2 = 1.00115965218059(13)` with source-stated `1 sigma` uncertainty. | The item already states the raw trial record, full covariance and weights are not reconstructed, no Gaussian/independence/posterior/coverage claim is added, and no QED comparison is proved. An electron-dipole EFT coefficient requires a separate matching and likelihood analysis. |
research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-2026-10-23/research-eft-experiments.md:129:| `exp-aqft-atlas-tau-squark-gluino-search-2025` | ATLAS Collaboration, EPJC 85 (2025) 1437, DOI 10.1140/epjc/s10052-025-14957-6. Search for RPC squark/gluino pair-production simplified models in tau(s)+jets+missing-transverse-momentum: 140 fb⁻¹ at 13 TeV (2015–18) plus 51.8 fb⁻¹ at 13.6 TeV (2022–23); three tau/lepton channels; independently optimized cut-and-count and ML strategies combined in profile-likelihood fits. Paper reports no significant overall deviation, observed 95% CLs exclusions reaching gluino 2.25 TeV / squark 1.7 TeV only in its specific simplified mass parameterizations. | The paper states model-specific spectra, branching fractions, narrow-width approximation, R-parity conservation, detector simulations, trigger selection, tau fake-factor background, jet/tau/lepton calibrations, correlated/uncorrelated nuisances, luminosity uncertainties, and asymptotic profile-likelihood validation. It also reports a locally most-compatible ML benchmark with `p_local=0.00058` (`Z=3.2`) while concluding there is no significant overall deviation; retain this local/background-fit detail and do not turn a local value or contour into a universal SUSY exclusion. Mass limits do not apply to all SUSY models or spectra. |
research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-2026-10-23/research-eft-experiments.md:142:| E. E. Jenkins, A. V. Manohar, M. Trott, SMEFT RGE I–III, arXiv:1308.2627, 1310.4838, 1312.2014 | Titles/abstracts and bibliographic records inspected; I–III divide scalar, Yukawa, and gauge terms of one-loop dimension-six anomalous dimensions. | Matrices and scheme conventions not independently checked here; source candidate only until exact sector, flavor and normalization are verified. |
research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-2026-10-23/research-eft-experiments.md:143:| G. Buchalla, O. Catà, C. Krause, “Complete Electroweak Chiral Lagrangian with a Light Higgs at NLO,” arXiv:1307.5017v3 | Abstract/introduction, pp. 1–2: nonlinear Goldstone coset, singlet light scalar, loop/chiral power counting, one-loop counterterms and NLO basis. | Detailed basis tables and coefficient conventions require focused read before local reuse. |
research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-2026-10-23/research-eft-experiments.md:144:| A. Adams et al., “Causality, Analyticity and an IR Obstruction to UV Completion,” arXiv:hep-th/0602178 | Abstract, forward-amplitude argument around §4 / pp. 14–20, and stated caveat near pp. 17–18: positivity follows under analyticity and high-energy growth assumptions; mass gap/IR regulator helps control the Froissart bound and massless cuts. | Their result is a specified shift-symmetric scalar example and related applications, not a universal theorem for every EFT, gauge amplitude, or gravity. |
research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-2026-10-23/research-eft-experiments.md:155:Keep definitions and finite, conditional mathematics upstream of QFT applications; build SMEFT/HEFT and supersymmetric operator classes only after the algebraic and power-counting contracts; derive matching/running after these contracts; use analyticity/positivity after the exact amplitude inputs are fixed; place measured EFT/SUSY outcomes as `experiment` items only after operational observables and likelihood/statistical methods are specified. An experiment can be a logical prerequisite only when a later physical theorem explicitly consumes its reported estimate as an empirical premise with conditions and uncertainty carried forward. Ordinary `supported_by`, `tested_by`, and `motivated_by` relationships remain outside the acyclic `deps` graph.
research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-2026-10-23/research-eft-experiments.md:159:The useful minimal mathematical sequence is: (1) formal series, finite-dimensional linear algebra, polynomial modules, Lie/reductive group actions and invariant quotients; (2) test-function/distribution and Fourier tools for local actions and regulated perturbative amplitudes; (3) finite-regulator Gaussian integration for the one existing exact shell model; (4) ODE existence and matrix evolution for explicitly truncated RG systems; (5) complex analysis/residue/dispersion integrals and a spectral/optical-theorem bridge for amplitude positivity; and (6) measurable probability, likelihoods, profile-likelihood ratio and coverage methods for reported inference. Missing bridges must be added as mathematical-domain items with mathematical-only dependencies or treated as open obligations. Physics postulates, model interpretations, detector calibration assumptions, and measured input remain physical/empirical interfaces.
research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-2026-10-23/research-gauge.md:5:The scope here is the geometric and mathematical development of non-Abelian Yang–Mills theory: principal bundles and connection forms; local gauge potentials and curvature; the classical Yang–Mills action; gauge fixing, Faddeev–Popov, BRST and BV; perturbative gauge-preserving renormalization; topological sectors and instantons; lattice observables and confinement; and the four-dimensional existence/mass-gap frontier. General EFT and anomaly-matching interfaces belong to the adjacent scaffold, while supersymmetry transformations, supermultiplets, BPS sectors, localization, and dualities belong to the supersymmetry scaffold. This note proposes a few shared gauge suppliers for those tracks but does not take ownership of their distinct results.
research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-2026-10-23/research-gauge.md:15:Every definition and result must use exact hypotheses and local arguments. Sources document the mathematical and physical context; a citation is not a proof supplier in active physics content. A locally authored theorem must prove its stated implication from the declared mathematical premises and physical postulates. A formal perturbation series is coefficientwise algebra and carries no convergence claim. A regulator result is not a continuum result. An established theorem whose proof is not written locally is an authoring obligation, not an open problem. Genuinely unresolved claims use an op- item, receive a dated formulation/status/source review, and never become logical suppliers.
research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-2026-10-23/research-gauge.md:24:| **def-principal-connection-and-vertical-curvature**; **def-gauge-group-of-a-smooth-principal-bundle**; **prop-gauge-transformations-act-on-principal-connections**; **prop-gauge-transformations-induce-associated-bundle-automorphisms** on the same page | Published and imported. The connection is a right-invariant horizontal complement \(TP=VP\oplus H\); its curvature is the vertical-valued tensor \(K_H(X,Y)=-v([hX,hY])\). The gauge group consists of smooth equivariant diffeomorphisms over \(\mathrm{id}_M\). Pushforward acts on horizontal connections and transports vertical curvature; a finite-dimensional representation gives the induced associated-bundle automorphism and section action. | The connection definition explicitly does not identify \(VP\) with \(\mathfrak g\), state a \(\mathfrak g\)-valued connection one-form, or give Cartan’s formula \(F=dA+\tfrac12[A\wedge A]\). The gauge-group definition assigns no topology or infinite-dimensional Lie-group structure. The connection and connection-action chain inherits the stated \(\mathrm{AC}_\omega\) assumptions; the gauge-group definition itself is choice-free. Carry each axiom only through consumers that actually use that supplier. |
research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-2026-10-23/research-gauge.md:40:| **physics/library/quantum-field-theory/qft-g02.md**: **post-qft-formal-qed-coefficients**, **post-qft-compact-lattice-gauge-model**, **pthm-qft-lattice-gauge-existence**, **pthm-qft-lattice-gauge-ward**; supporting **def-qft-compact-lattice-gauge-data** | The finite lattice model is a finite oriented graph with compact \(U(1)\) rotors on links, finite CAR matter, integer electric operators, an explicit Hamiltonian domain and Gauss operators. Its published physical theorems establish a nonzero finite-regulator Gauss sector, unitary dynamics and selected finite-regulator Ward/Gauss identities under their stated assumptions. | This is not non-Abelian \(G\)-valued link data, not an infinite lattice theorem, not a continuum limit, not interacting continuum QED, not a proof of confinement, and not a Yang–Mills existence or mass-gap supplier. The formal QED coefficients are not a convergent series or an all-loop gauge-independence theorem. |
research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-2026-10-23/research-gauge.md:41:| **physics/items/def-qft-qed-gauge-data.md**; **physics/items/post-qft-qed-local-coupling.md**; **physics/items/lem-qft-qed-tree-ward.md**; **physics/items/lem-qft-qed-conserved-current-gauge.md** | Published U(1) flat-space charged Dirac/Maxwell conventions, smooth local gauge covariance, and the listed finite tree-current identities. The item contracts state metric, SI/natural units, smooth field domains and explicit scope. | These are Abelian; the tree identities do not establish loop Ward identities or non-Abelian Slavnov–Taylor identities. The local coupling postulate does not quantize the interacting classical action. |
research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-2026-10-23/research-gauge.md:42:| **physics/library/quantum-field-theory-mathematics/qftx-bv-brst.md**: **def-qftx-abelian-local-brst**, **lem-qftx-brst-nilpotence-doublets**, **def-qftx-brst-relative-local-cohomology**, **prop-qftx-anomaly-obstruction** | Published mathematical definitions and results for a finite-jet Abelian BRST algebra, its nonminimal doublets, compactly supported relative local cohomology, and a conditional obstruction-class statement. The local differential, parity, ghost numbers, total derivative, local support and counterterm subcomplex are explicit. | The nonminimal doublet lemma is proved for the Abelian complex. The anomaly proposition assumes a formal nilpotent Ward operator, local breaking, a selected admissible counterterm complex and a scalar time-ordering supplier; it does not prove a quantum action principle or give a non-Abelian anomaly calculation. |
research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-2026-10-23/research-gauge.md:43:| **physics/library/quantum-field-theory-mathematics/qftx-anomaly-cocycles.md**: **def-qftx-loop-current-cocycle**, **prop-qftx-loop-cocycle-jacobi**, **def-qftx-chiral-anomaly-interface** | Published current-algebra and chiral-anomaly interface definitions, with exact hypotheses and separate representation-theoretic dependencies. | The page is an interface and conditional algebraic input; it is not the complete non-Abelian gauge anomaly classification or an anomaly-cancellation theorem for an unspecified matter spectrum. |
research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-2026-10-23/research-gauge.md:44:| **physics/library/quantum-field-theory-mathematics/qftx-causal-renormalization.md** and **qftx-renormalization-hopf.md** | Published scalar causal-extension/finite-renormalization results and a combinatorial rooted-forest/Hopf subtraction interface. Exact local-polynomial, microcausality, graph-scaling, and subtraction-algebra claims are reusable when their own premises fit. | The causal induction is explicitly scalar; the Hopf-character factorization does not construct a gauge theory, impose Slavnov–Taylor identities, remove a gauge anomaly, or make a perturbative series converge. |
