- Claim/conventions: fixes flat oriented \\(\mathbb R^{1,3}\\), signature \\((-+++ )\\), natural units, trivial smooth SU(3) and U(1) backgrounds, the positive-chirality Weyl field space, mass dimensions, the \\(\mathbf3_{+1}\\)/\\(\bar{\mathbf3}_{-1}\\) conjugate pair used by the theorem, anti-Hermitian connections, the common Pauli–Villars scale, consistent descent convention, admitted counterterms, and compact-support boundary conditions. The determinant-to-polynomial relation is the explicit source-backed large-mass Pauli–Villars triangle input to this selected formal regulator datum, not a local derivation or a generic regulator theorem. The background relative cohomology is restricted to the finite-jet algebra of $A,B$ and their ghosts, so its counterterm space matches the declared background-only local counterterms.
- Dependencies/level: `def-aqft-thooft-anomaly` (formulation, in-run level 0), the p-form definition, local BRST cohomology, non-Abelian BRST complex and nilpotence lemma (external suppliers), and the cubic polynomial (in-run level 0); `dependency_level: 1`.
- Sources/disposition: Bilal §§5, 7, 9, and 10 and Alvarez §§2.1–2.4 support the exact one-loop descent input and convention boundary. The data definition asserts no global anomaly conclusion, mixed gravitational term, or continuum construction.
- Next action: author the selected-spectrum theorem and B examples against these exact data, preserving the one-loop and local-only qualifications.

### `pthm-aqft-selected-chiral-spectrum-anomaly-cancellation`

- Claim/conventions: conditionally proves vanishing of the infinitesimal, one-loop local anomaly class for two positive-chirality Weyl species in (E=(\mathbf3,+1)) and (E^*=(\bar{\mathbf3},-1)) under nondynamical (SU(3)\times U(1)_V) backgrounds on flat (\mathbb R^{1,3}). The determinant-to-descent law is an explicit source-backed Pauli–Villars input. No global, torsion, dynamical-gauge, or continuum claim is made.
- Dependencies/level: `def-aqft-anomaly-matching-data` (formulation, in-run level 1), `def-aqft-thooft-anomaly` (formulation, level 0), the dual-polynomial lemma (in-run level 1), and the relative-counterterm lemma (level 0); the maximum in-run supplier level is 1, so `dependency_level: 2`.
- Proof route: additivity of the common consistent descent, exact dual-representation trace/transgression cancellation, passage to the local relative class, and preservation under admitted counterterms. The proof does not infer the determinant law from classical BRST nilpotence or a representation coefficient alone.
- Sources/disposition: Bilal §§5, 7, 9, 10 and Alvarez §§2.1–2.4 support the adopted physical input and conventions. The cancellation itself is derived from the local matrix identities. No external model/global-anomaly result is imported.
- Next action: author the three worked B-page examples; then build the manifest, contracts and source coverage from the completed carriers.

### `ex-aqft-vectorlike-conjugate-chiral-pair`

- Claim/conventions: expands the selected (E=(\mathbf3,+1)) polynomial into pure SU(3), mixed (U(1)_V\)-SU(3)(^2), and pure (U(1)_V^3) terms, then checks their cancellation with the dual species and common descent.
- Dependencies/level: anomaly-matching data (formulation, 4), cubic-polynomial definition (mathematical, 0), dual-polynomial lemma (mathematical, 1), and the A-page physics theorem (physical result, 5); `dependency_level: 6`.
- Next action: author the one-species polynomial example and the local counterterm-shift example, then reconcile the B manifest.

### `ex-aqft-single-chiral-fundamental-polynomial`

- Claim/conventions: verifies that a single positive-chirality (E=(\mathbf3,+1)) species has a nonzero degree-six polynomial under the selected regulator; a concrete formal six-dimensional two-form witness shows nonzero. It explicitly makes no claim that the corresponding relative class is nontrivial or globally anomalous.
- Dependencies/level: anomaly-matching data (formulation, level 4) and cubic-polynomial definition (mathematical, level 0); `dependency_level: 5`.
- Next action: finish the counterterm example and run the source-coverage/check pass.

### `ex-aqft-mixed-background-counterterm-shift`

- Claim/conventions: for trivial flat SU(3) and (U(1)_V) backgrounds, the local term (\lambda B\wedge\operatorname{tr}(A\wedge dA+\frac23A^3)) shifts the (U(1)_V) representative by (-\lambda\alpha\operatorname{tr}(F_A^2)) modulo a compact-support boundary term. The example does not claim that the full combined anomaly is removed or that the SU(3) representative is unchanged.
- Dependencies/level: anomaly-matching data (formulation, level 4), local anomaly definition (formulation, level 3), and the relative-coboundary lemma (mathematical, level 3); `dependency_level: 5`.
- Next action: finish any source/statement corrections, create frontmatter-only pages and the exact item manifest mirrors, then build contracts and coverage.


