items/def-qftx-instanton-equivariant-partition-series.md:57:It has no asserted analytic convergence. In the source's Euclidean convention the real mass $m_E$ has mass dimension one, $m=i m_E$, and the equivariant mass is $\widetilde m=m+(\epsilon_1+\epsilon_2)/2$. For the adopted round $S^4_r$ model, $N=2$, $\epsilon_1=\epsilon_2=r^{-1}$, and hence $\widetilde m=i m_E+r^{-1}$. This mass shift is a source-qualified convention. The S4 postulate assumes a supersymmetry-compatible noncommutative regulator agreeing near each pole with the flat-space regulator; it does not construct that regulator or a continuum path-integral measure.
